<title>UK: Psion replaces Blenheim in FTSE-250.</title>
<headline>Psion replaces Blenheim in FTSE-250.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hand-held computers firm Psion Plc will replace exhibitions organiser Blenheim Group in the UK's FTSE 250 share index, with effect from the close of business today, the FTSE Actuaries UK Indices Committee said on Monday.</p>
<p>It said the move follows Blenheim's takeover by United News &amp; Media. Psion also becomes a constituent of the FTSE 350 Lower Yield Index and will be removed from the FTSE SmallCap Index.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
